WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.418
The vault earns its keep when things come out of it.

00:00:03.518 --> 00:00:07.220
A knowledge base that only answers questions is a reference book.

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:11.622
Articles, reports, decisions, understanding.

00:00:12.822 --> 00:00:15.948
Writing starts from concept pages, not a prompt.

00:00:16.048 --> 00:00:22.582
Outline from what we read. Cite our sources. Keep our voice. Close the loop.

00:00:23.132 --> 00:00:28.923
A report starts with what the vault covers. The question. What we found.

00:00:28.973 --> 00:00:34.370
Where sources disagree. What we could not establish. What would change it.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.046
Publishing should be opt-in.

00:00:37.096 --> 00:00:41.251
Under opt-out, one forgotten flag publishes something private.

00:00:41.301 --> 00:00:44.550
With publish true, nothing without it leaves.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:49.447
Never export the whole vault to a format we cannot regenerate.

00:00:49.497 --> 00:00:51.490
The markdown is the artifact.

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:58.580
Last, learning. Ask questions from our pages. Answer without looking.

00:00:58.630 --> 00:01:02.558
Find what we never digested. Explain it back.

00:01:03.108 --> 00:01:08.442
That's chapter eight, outputs. Start with page one: Writing from the vault.
